course: dictionary
lesson: 247
title: Alp and the Alps
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An alp is a high mountain, especially a snowy one. When it has a capital letter, the Alps is a name: the great range of high mountains across Europe. Look for clues in the sentences around it.
explain: «The Rhine flows from the Swiss Alps to the North Sea.» Swiss tells you the Alps are in Switzerland, and the river starts high up and flows all the way down to the sea. Next, «Ötzi's body was kept by the ice of the Alps.» Ice tells you the Alps are cold and snowy.
explain: Now test your meaning. «Hannibal crossed the Alps with elephants.» Swap in high mountains: Hannibal crossed high mountains with elephants. It makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: The Alps is a range of high mountains in Europe, running through France, Switzerland, Italy, Austria and other countries.
fact: An alp can also mean a high mountain meadow in Switzerland, where cows graze in summer.
fact: The Alps include famous peaks such as Mont Blanc and the Matterhorn.
fact: Long ago, the army leader Hannibal of Carthage crossed the Alps with elephants, and Rome fought him.
fact: The Alps are one of the places where glaciers, huge slow rivers of ice, can be found.
exercise: «Hannibal crossed the Alps with elephants.» What is the Alps? | A desert with hot sand | A deep lake where fish live | *A great range of high mountains in Europe | A busy city port
exercise: «The Rhine flows from the Swiss Alps to the North Sea.» Which country is the Swiss Alps in? | Brazil | *Switzerland | Egypt | Canada
exercise: «Ötzi's body was kept by the ice of the Alps.» What does the ice tell you about the Alps? | They are flat and sandy | They are under the sea | They are hot and dry | *They are cold and snowy
test: In Switzerland, what is an alp? | A kind of tall tree | *A high mountain meadow where cows graze in summer | A town with a busy port | A deep cave under the sea
test: Mont Blanc and the Matterhorn are famous peaks in which range? | The Sahara | *The Alps | The Rockies | The Himalayas
exam: In «Rome fought Hannibal, who crossed the Alps with elephants», what does Alps mean? | A type of bread | A small wooden boat | A loud noise | *A great range of high mountains
